  "vaultRuleDecisions": {
    "seed": {
      "reason": "rmUSDC is seeded with 1 USDC (SEED_DEPOSIT_USDC) to the seed share receiver (owner D3, 2026-10-01). The baskets take no seed: the 18-decimal virtual share offset protects every basket (issue 1705 Q6 (a)).",
      "decision": "https://github.com/robotmoney/robotmoney-core/issues/1705"
    },
    "eligibilitySource": {
      "reason": "rmUSDC is the router's base leg: the router stage makes it eligible and sets the first default vector before any basket exists. Each basket stage makes itself eligible from the sheet's ROUTER_DEFAULT_BPS in one migrateEligibility, and the last one leaves exactly the sheet's ROUTER_WEIGHTS, which names all four vaults (ADR-0018). Issue 1705 Q4 (a) fixes the sheet format: ELIGIBLE_VAULTS=PROTO,RWA,HARD with rmUSDC in ROUTER_WEIGHTS, the same on the Twin chain and on 8453 (docs/technical/governance-isomorphism.md 1.1).",
      "decision": "https://github.com/robotmoney/robotmoney-core/issues/1705"
    },
    "emergencyLevers": {
      "reason": "The two vault families have different emergency levers, each callable by EMERGENCY_ROLE (the emergency key) with no timelock. None freezes a withdrawal. For the mainnet test the levers stay as they are and are named here per vault (issue 1705 Q2 (a)). Only rmUSDC can take a position out of NAV: emergencyExcludeAdapter (exclude-only) and forceRemoveAdapter each open an exclusion record that snapshots the share supply, and recoverRemovedAdapter pays a force-removed adapter back into that record tranche by tranche. A recovery is credited pro rata to the holders at the snapshot (core 1820, security review 2026-10-15 SR-1015-21 and SR-1015-27), never to whoever holds shares at that moment; a holder who exits meanwhile is paid at the reduced NAV and keeps the claim. Restoring an excluded adapter stays ADMIN_ROLE, through the timelock. Narrowing the levers is decided before the final deployment.",
      "decision": "https://github.com/robotmoney/robotmoney-core/issues/1705"
    }
  },
